      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm running into some really inconsistent behavior in our ETL pipeline that I can't quite pin down. We're seeing a lot of `SettingWithCopyWarning` messages popping up in our transformation scripts, but the actual outcome is unpredictable.\n\nSometimes the original dataframe is updated correctly, and other times the change is lost entirely because it was applied to a copy. It feels like the warning is signaling some kind of non-deterministic behavior in how pandas handles the underlying memory during slicing.\n\nCould you explain the technical reason why this is so inconsistent? I need to know if there's a specific pattern that causes pandas to switch between returning a view and a copy, because right now the behavior feels almost \"unpredictable\" or like it's happening behind the scenes without a clear logic.",
